WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.535
Brody peeled off the rest of his armor as the horses galloped toward the Temple of Caerus.

2
00:00:08.536 --> 00:00:12.323
"Did you bring our regular clothes?" he asked Julia.

3
00:00:12.324 --> 00:00:16.284
Then he blinked, realizing she'd already changed.

4
00:00:16.285 --> 00:00:23.089
She handed over his clothes. "Hurry," she said, glancing back over her shoulder.

5
00:00:23.090 --> 00:00:26.934
"It won't take long for the gods to catch up to us."

6
00:00:26.935 --> 00:00:31.043
"Only if they figure out where you're going," Heracles said.

7
00:00:31.044 --> 00:00:34.212
"Do you think they will?" Brody asked.

8
00:00:34.213 --> 00:00:42.516
Julia shrugged. "Hermes or Caerus will certainly figure it out. But will they tell Zeus and Hera?"

9
00:00:42.517 --> 00:00:50.428
"I doubt it," Heracles said. "Hermes and Caerus won't wish to help Zeus or Hera under the circumstances."

10
00:00:50.429 --> 00:00:55.626
Brody hoped Heracles was right.

11
00:00:55.627 --> 00:01:03.702
Soon Iphicles pulled sharply on the reins, and the chariot skidded to a stop at the bottom of the temple's steps.

12
00:01:03.703 --> 00:01:09.741
"Thanks for the ride," Julia called as she and Brody climbed out.

13
00:01:09.742 --> 00:01:16.199
She looked at Heracles."Is it safe for you two to return to the Games?"

14
00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:20.199
"I think you'll be fine once we're gone," Brody said.

15
00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:23.209
"Zeus will protect you from Hera, Heracles.

16
00:01:23.210 --> 00:01:27.400
And he probably wants to crown you with that olive wreath!"

17
00:01:27.401 --> 00:01:32.120
"The festivities can wait." Heracles climbed out too.

18
00:01:32.121 --> 00:01:34.986
"I want to make sure you two get home safely.

19
00:01:34.987 --> 00:01:37.888
How will you get past the temple guard?"

20
00:01:37.889 --> 00:01:41.380
"We'll be fine," Brody said.

21
00:01:41.381 --> 00:01:47.987
"I insist," Heracles said firmly. "Come on, Iphicles."

22
00:01:47.988 --> 00:01:55.828
"If you say so, brother." Iphicles got out of the chariot and tied the horses to a tree.

23
00:01:55.829 --> 00:01:59.073
There was no guard outside the temple.

24
00:01:59.074 --> 00:02:04.416
"Good!" Brody said. "Modern times, here we come!"

25
00:02:04.417 --> 00:02:13.307
He charged through the temple's outer room and through the entrance to the inner room. The passage was still open.

26
00:02:13.308 --> 00:02:18.515
"Whew!" Brody exclaimed. "Hurry up, Julia. We don't want to—"

27
00:02:18.516 --> 00:02:22.112
A sudden flash of bright light interrupted him.

28
00:02:22.113 --> 00:02:27.449
Brody shaded his eyes and coughed at the smoke that suddenly filled the chamber.

29
00:02:27.450 --> 00:02:32.682
When the smoke cleared, Hera stood between Brody and the rift.

30
00:02:32.683 --> 00:02:40.979
"Oh, good," she said with a sneer. "I was hoping I wasn't too late to see you off, mortals."

31
00:02:40.980 --> 00:02:44.781
Julia ran in with Heracles and his brother.

32
00:02:44.782 --> 00:02:49.735
"Hera, leave them alone!" Heracles called. "They've done nothing."

33
00:02:49.736 --> 00:02:59.391
Hera ignored him. "Come here, mortal," she said, reaching for Iphicles and pulling him toward her.

34
00:02:59.392 --> 00:03:03.487
Brody expected Iphicles to struggle to free himself.

35
00:03:03.488 --> 00:03:08.363
But Iphicles just stood there as Hera stroked his hair.

36
00:03:08.364 --> 00:03:13.585
"You have my thanks, mortal boy," the goddess purred.

37
00:03:13.586 --> 00:03:21.293
"Without your information I might not have learned all of your friends' secrets until it was too late."

38
00:03:21.294 --> 00:03:25.953
"Huh?" Brody said, not understanding what she meant.

39
00:03:25.954 --> 00:03:35.425
But Julia was scowling. "I hate to tell you this, Brody," she exclaimed, "but Iphicles betrayed us!"

40
00:03:35.426 --> 00:03:45.842
"Don't flatter yourself," Iphicles snapped. "It wasn't you two I was after." He glared at Heracles.

41
00:03:45.843 --> 00:03:49.046
Now Brody was starting to follow along.

42
00:03:49.047 --> 00:03:56.710
"Wait . . . you betrayed your own brother, Iphicles?" he blurted out. "That's low!"

43
00:03:56.711 --> 00:04:03.910
Hera chuckled. "It's all a matter of perspective, mortal. I

44
00:04:03.911 --> 00:04:15.500
consider Iphicles a hero. He informed me about where I might have a moment alone with my husband's mortal champion. I

45
00:04:15.501 --> 00:04:20.282
couldn't rely on the other gods to destroy Heracles." Brody

46
00:04:20.283 --> 00:04:27.326
shuddered. Once again Hera had put extra emphasis on the word "mortal." Brody

47
00:04:27.327 --> 00:04:32.069
guessed that meant she knew that Heracles was half god. Julia

48
00:04:32.070 --> 00:04:41.250
was still glaring at Iphicles. "How could you do this?" she said. "Heracles is your own brother." Iphicles

49
00:04:41.251 --> 00:04:45.643
shrugged. "It was easy for me to do it. I've

50
00:04:45.644 --> 00:04:49.697
been hearing about the wonderful Alcides for my whole life. What

51
00:04:49.698 --> 00:04:55.051
about me? Nobody ever pays the slightest attention to me." "That's

52
00:04:55.052 --> 00:04:59.534
no reason to betray him to Hera!" Brody retorted. Heracles

53
00:04:59.535 --> 00:05:08.898
hadn't said a word yet. He stared at his brother with hurt in his eyes. Then his expression darkened. "If

54
00:05:08.899 --> 00:05:13.211
you had a problem with me, brother, you should have said so," he said. "Now

55
00:05:13.212 --> 00:05:16.488
you've put our friends in danger." "They're

56
00:05:16.489 --> 00:05:24.100
your friends, Heracles, not mine," Iphicles said. "I don't have any friends." "Say

57
00:05:24.101 --> 00:05:28.553
good-bye to them, Heracles," Hera spoke up. "Well,

58
00:05:28.554 --> 00:05:35.328
unless you wish me to send them to somewhere like Tartarus along with you." Brody's

59
00:05:35.329 --> 00:05:40.077
heart pounded. He didn't want to go to Tartarus! He

60
00:05:40.078 --> 00:05:43.036
didn't want Heracles to go there either. "Wait

61
00:05:43.037 --> 00:05:48.436
a minute!" Julia blurted out. "You can't send Heracles to Tartarus." Sparks

62
00:05:48.437 --> 00:05:53.055
shot out of Hera's eyes as she glared at Julia. "Who

63
00:05:53.056 --> 00:05:59.054
are you to tell me what I can or cannot do?" "You

64
00:05:59.055 --> 00:06:03.838
made a bet," Julia said, her voice shaking. "According

65
00:06:03.839 --> 00:06:14.135
to the bet, you were only allowed to send Heracles to Tartarus if he lost at least one event at the Games. And he won them all." Brody

66
00:06:14.136 --> 00:06:21.481
was impressed. Julia was standing up to Hera—and Hera was scary! Hera

67
00:06:21.482 --> 00:06:32.239
stared down at Julia. "You're right, my fellow gods were not able to stop Zeus' mighty hero in the Games. Unfortunately,

68
00:06:32.240 --> 00:06:37.693
that means he's safe from Tartarus." "Whew!"

69
00:06:37.694 --> 00:06:40.326
Brody thought. But

70
00:06:40.327 --> 00:06:48.827
Hera wasn't finished. "That doesn't mean he's completely safe, however." She sneered. "I

71
00:06:48.828 --> 00:06:57.414
can toss him somewhere much worse than Tartarus—like into the terrible future world beyond this rift." She

72
00:06:57.415 --> 00:07:01.513
pointed a long, thin finger at the time passage. Brody

73
00:07:01.514 --> 00:07:08.501
gasped. "But if you throw him through there, the rift will close!" he blurted out. "Yes,

74
00:07:08.502 --> 00:07:15.912
that's what my young mortal friend tells me." Hera patted Iphicles again. "It

75
00:07:15.913 --> 00:07:27.074
means that I won't be bothered by the mighty Heracles ever again." She let out a terrible cackle. "And

76
00:07:27.075 --> 00:07:40.387
he will surely suffer in that new place—because he'll know that his mortal friends are trapped here in Olympia forever!" "No!"

77
00:07:40.388 --> 00:07:45.425
Heracles cried. He leaped forward and grabbed at Hera. But

78
00:07:45.426 --> 00:07:48.280
the goddess was too quick for him. Tilting

79
00:07:48.281 --> 00:07:52.741
her staff forward, she shot out a bolt of energy. It

80
00:07:52.742 --> 00:07:57.046
struck Heracles in the chest and sent him hurtling backward. Heracles

81
00:07:57.047 --> 00:08:04.772
flew through the rift, and it closed with a snap !

